Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:50:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 329/488] Chat completions: the DeepSeek API's top-level
 thinking switch

DeepSeek's API turns thinking off with a top-level
"thinking": {"type": "disabled"}; deepseek-recipe accepts the same field. The
request dropped it, so DeepSeek-format clients always got reasoning
(christopherowen/spark-ds41f#447, reported by Acermax).

ChatCompletionRequest takes thinking {"type": "enabled" | "disabled"} and sets
both template spellings, thinking and enable_thinking, so a reasoning_effort
beside it cannot turn thinking back on; explicit chat_template_kwargs keep
precedence. An unknown type is rejected.

Tests: the request mapping, and the V4.1 tokenizer rendering the same prompt
for thinking {"type": "disabled"} as for chat_template_kwargs thinking false,
also beside reasoning_effort high.
